    <script type="application/ld+json">{"mainEntity":{"headline":"Characterization and Source Identification of Particulate Matter Over Srinagar (Garhwal) in Central Himalayan Region","description":"A comprehensive year-long characterization of PM2.5 collected during January-December 2017 at Srinagar (Garhwal) in the Central Himalayas, to investigate the seasonal variability, chemical composition, aerosol neutralization characteristics, and potential emission sources.. The annual mean PM2.5 concentration (80.01 ± 19.41 μg m⁻3), exceeded both national and international air-quality guidelines, with maximum aerosol loading during winter and minimum concentration during the monsoon. Water-soluble ionic species accounted for approximately 41.3% of the PM₂.₅ mass, with sulfate (7.36 μg m⁻3) dominating the ionic composition, followed by chloride (6.81 μg m⁻3), sodium (5.36 μg m⁻3), and ammonium (3.13 μg m⁻3), indicating the importance of secondary inorganic aerosols together with crustal and combustion-derived contributions. Neutralization analysis revealed that aerosols remained predominantly alkaline throughout the year, while chloride depletion analysis revealed extensive atmospheric aging of marine aerosols during long-range transport, with maximum depletion (33.91%) occurring during post-monsoon months coinciding with peak sulfate concentrations (13.55 μg m⁻3). Principal Component Analysis (PCA) suggested three probable source influences explaining 75.54% of total variance: long-range transported aged aerosols mixed with crustal dust (41.33%), combustion emissions (21.04%) and episodic agricultural and crustal influences (13.17%). These findings reflect the Central Himalayan foothills as a key transitional receptor of regional aerosols and provide a scientific basis for air-quality management in this environmentally sensitive region.","datePublished":"2026-09-11T00:00:00Z","dateModified":"2026-09-11T00:00:00Z","pageStart":"1","pageEnd":"19","sameAs":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11270-026-09930-2","keywords":["Fine particulate matter (PM2.5)","Seasonal variability","Principal Component Analysis (PCA)","Himalayan environment","Environment","general","Water Quality/Water Pollution","Atmospheric Protection/Air Quality Control/Air Pollution","Soil Science & Conservation","Hydrogeology","Climate Change/Climate Change Impacts"],"image":["https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs11270-026-09930-2/MediaObjects/11270_2026_9930_Fig1_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs11270-026-09930-2/MediaObjects/11270_2026_9930_Fig2_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs11270-026-09930-2/MediaObjects/11270_2026_9930_Fig3_HTML.jpg","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs11270-026-09930-2/MediaObjects/11270_2026_9930_Fig4_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs11270-026-09930-2/MediaObjects/11270_2026_9930_Fig5_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs11270-026-09930-2/MediaObjects/11270_2026_9930_Fig6_HTML.png"],"isPartOf":{"name":"Water, Air, & Soil Pollution","issn":["1573-2932","0049-6979"],"volumeNumber":"237","@type":["Periodical","PublicationVolume"]},"publisher":{"name":"Springer International Publishing","logo":{"url":"https://www.springernature.com/app-sn/public/images/logo-springernature.png","@type":"ImageObject"},"@type":"Organization"},"author":[{"name":"D. S. Bisht","affiliation":[{"name":"Indian Institute of Tropical Meteorology","address":{"name":"Ministry of Earth Sciences, Indian Institute of Tropical Meteorology, New Delhi, India","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"}],"email":"dsbisht@tropmet.res.in","@type":"Person"},{"name":"S. G. Krishna","affiliation":[{"name":"Indian Institute of Tropical Meteorology","address":{"name":"Ministry of Earth Sciences, Indian Institute of Tropical Meteorology, New Delhi, India","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"}],"@type":"Person"},{"name":"A. S. Gautam","affiliation":[{"name":"HNB Garhwal University","address":{"name":"Department of Physics, HNB Garhwal University, Srinagar, India","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"}],"@type":"Person"},{"name":"R. S. Negi","affiliation":[{"name":"HNB Garhwal University","address":{"name":"Department of Rural Technology, HNB Garhwal University, Srinagar, India","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"}],"@type":"Person"},{"name":"V. Singh","affiliation":[{"name":"Indian Institute of Tropical Meteorology","address":{"name":"Ministry of Earth Sciences, Indian Institute of Tropical Meteorology, New Delhi, India","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"}],"@type":"Person"},{"name":"A. K. Srivastava","affiliation":[{"name":"Indian Institute of Tropical Meteorology","address":{"name":"Ministry of Earth Sciences, Indian Institute of Tropical Meteorology, New Delhi, India","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"},{"name":"Academy of Scientific and Innovative Research (AcSIR), Uttar Pradesh","address":{"name":"Academy of Scientific and Innovative Research (AcSIR), Uttar Pradesh, Ghaziabad, India","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"}],"@type":"Person"},{"name":"N. Rao","affiliation":[{"name":"Indian Institute of Tropical Meteorology","address":{"name":"Ministry of Earth Sciences, Indian Institute of Tropical Meteorology, New Delhi, India","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"}],"@type":"Person"},{"name":"V. Anand","affiliation":[{"name":"Indian Institute of Tropical Meteorology","address":{"name":"Ministry of Earth Sciences, Indian Institute of Tropical Meteorology, New Delhi, India","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"}],"@type":"Person"},{"name":"M. P. Raju","affiliation":[{"name":"Amity Institute of Environment and Sustainability, Amity University Uttar Pradesh (AUUP)","address":{"name":"Department of Climate Change and Environmental Sustainability, Amity Institute of Environment and Sustainability, Amity University Uttar Pradesh (AUUP), Noida, India","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"}],"@type":"Person"},{"name":"A. S. Panicker","affiliation":[{"name":"Indian Institute of Tropical Meteorology","address":{"name":"Ministry of Earth Sciences, Indian Institute of Tropical Meteorology, New Delhi, India","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"}],"email":"panicker@tropmet.res.in","@type":"Person"},{"name":"S. Ghude","affiliation":[{"name":"Indian Institute of Tropical Meteorology","address":{"name":"Ministry of Earth Sciences, Indian Institute of Tropical Meteorology, New Delhi, India","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"}],"@type":"Person"}],"isAccessibleForFree":false,"hasPart":{"isAccessibleForFree":false,"cssSelector":".main-content","@type":"WebPageElement"},"@type":"ScholarlyArticle"},"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"WebPage"}</script>

        
        
